{"t": 1794110163.1458833, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "checkout / PaymentGatewayErrors (AG-7731) \u2014 root cause found.\n\nGateway API v2026-11 (\"strict amounts\") now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). checkout was sending decimal euros (e.g. 12.34), so charges were rejected with HTTP 400 `invalid_amount` \u2014 hence the 38% gateway 4xx rate since 07:41 UTC.\n\nFix: checkout/gateway.py `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (ROUND_HALF_UP, no float artifacts). Verified: 12.34 -> {\"amount\": 1234, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}.\n\nNeeds a deploy to prod-eu-1; 4xx rate should drop once the new build is serving traffic."}, "ok": true}
